    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: derive `ageBand` from `birthDate`\n\nThe spec required `POST /api/owners` to accept an optional ISO `birthDate` and expose an `ageBand` (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) computed against the owner's `registrationDate`. The acceptance test creates an owner with a `birthDate` and then reads `ageBand` back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the value has to survive a round-trip through storage.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing convention for read-derived fields (`contactPreference`, `locality`, `membershipLevel` \u2014 all computed in the mapper from stored data via a small `util` class), rather than adding a new pipeline step and a stored column for a value that's fully derivable:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (input, and round-tripped like `registrationDate`) and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it in from the request DTO automatically.\n3. **`util/AgeBand.java`** \u2014 new single-responsibility helper: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` \u2192 `<18 MINOR`, `18\u201364 ADULT`, `65+ SENIOR`; returns `null` when either date is absent.\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"java(ageBand(owner))\")` delegating to `AgeBand.of(owner)`, mirroring the other derived-field defaults.\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to `owners`.\n\nBecause `ageBand` is derived from the stored `birthDate` and `registrationDate`, it's correct for both the create response and subsequent `GET`s, with no duplicated logic. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
